TI  - Nephrotic syndrome at 5 months: no definitive treatment or complications for 12 
      years.
PG  - 604-6
AB  - We describe a patient who developed nephrotic syndrome at 5 months, with 
      extensive glomerular and tubular damage on biopsy. The patient was treated with 
      diuretics and was asymptomatic for a decade despite unremitting proteinuria. A 
      repeat biopsy at 13 years of age showed remarkable healing with histopathological 
      features consistent with "minimal change" nephrotic syndrome. This patient 
      illustrates a favorable clinical outcome, without specific treatment, of 
      nephrotic syndrome of long duration.
