TI  - Treatment of arterial hypertension in the elderly using enalapril.
PG  - 333-7
AB  - BACKGROUND: Arterial pressure increases with age and is the most common chronic 
      disease in the elderly, men and women alike. At present arterial hypertension is 
      considered a social disease as it poses great health, economic and social 
      problems. METHODS: A group of 50 patients of both sexes, between 66 and 83 years 
      of age, suffering from essential arterial hypertension and treated with Enalapril 
      administered at doses varying from 10 to 20 mg/day, for a period of 18 months, 
      has been studied. RESULTS AND CONCLUSIONS: The results of this study showed that 
      blood pressure values of almost all the patients treated normalised and left 
      ventricular hypertrophy decreased in all patients with this complication.
