TI  - Effect of angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor on cardiopulmonary baroreflex 
      sensitivity in patients with acute myocardial infarction.
PG  - 1241-4, A6
AB  - We evaluated the effect of angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibition (quinapril) 
      on cardiopulmonary baroreflex sensitivity in 30 patients with uncomplicated 
      myocardial infarction (quinapril group, 15 patients; placebo group, 15 patients) 
      at 5 and 10 days after the onset of myocardial infarction. This study indicates 
      that quinapril improved cardiopulmonary baroreflex and thus reduced sympathetic 
      outflow in patients with acute myocardial infarction.
