TI  - Drug-related pemphigus and angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitors.
PG  - 242-6
AB  - A 105-year-old woman developed pemphigus foliaceus. She had been on fosinopril, 
      an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor (ACE inhibitor) for 4 years. 
      Anti-intercellular cement substance antibodies were positive with titre > 160. 
      She died during admission of an unrelated illness. A 57-year-old man developed 
      pemphigus vulgaris after 11 months treatment with quinapril. At 14 months after 
      developing pemphigus, this man continues on prednisone and azathioprine. We 
      speculate that these are cases of ACE-inhibitor-related pemphigus and we review 
      ACE-inhibitor-related pemphigus.
