TI  - Angiotensin converting enzyme inhibitor induced hyperkalaemic paralysis.
PG  - 114-5
AB  - Secondary hyperkalaemic paralysis is a rare condition often mimicking the 
      Guillain-Barre syndrome. There have been a few case reports of hyperkalaemia 
      caused by renal failure, trauma, and drugs where the presentation has been with 
      muscle weakness. A case of hyperkalaemic paralysis caused by an angiotensin 
      converting enzyme inhibitor is reported.
