TI  - Effect of quinapril on intimal hyperplasia after coronary stenting as assessed by 
      intravascular ultrasound.
PG  - 443-5, A6
AB  - We studied whether angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibition with quinapril 
      treatment can prevent in-stent restenosis after successful implantation of 
      Palmaz-Schatz stents. Intravascular ultrasound study, but not quantitative 
      coronary angiography analysis, revealed that quinapril treatment significantly 
      prevented the loss of both minimal lumen cross-sectional area and lumen volume in 
      stents, in addition to reducing the increase in intimal hyperplasia volume.
