TI  - Are angiotensin II receptor blockers more efficacious than placebo in heart 
      failure? Implications of ELITE-2. Evaluation of Losartan In The Elderly.
PG  - 606-7, A9
AB  - In the light of the recent randomized controlled trials in chronic heart failure, 
      it is now commonly assumed that treatment with an angiotensin-receptor blocker 
      (ARB) is equivalent to treatment with an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) 
      inhibitor. We performed an imputed placebo analysis using previous placebo-ACE 
      inhibitor trials and the current ACE inhibitor-ARB comparison studies, which 
      shows that ARBs may not even be superior to placebos, let alone an ACE inhibitor.
