TI  - [Reversible impairment of renal function during treatment with lisinopril, an 
      ACE-inhibitor (case report)].
PG  - 245-8
AB  - ACE inhibitors are group of drugs whose use over the last ten years has largely 
      expanded. New members of this group of drugs are developed and registered and 
      today in Croatia exist a dozen ACE inhibitors from different pharmaceutical 
      companies like lisinopril, cilazapril, ramipril, trandolapril, enalapril etc. 
      Notable side effects of ACE inhibitors are: hypotension, dry cough, rash, 
      angioneurotical edema, impaired renal function and acute renal failure. The aim 
      of the article was to present a 72 year old patient with reversible impairment of 
      renal function during treatment with ACE inhibitor lisinopril.
