TI  - Current treatment and future directions in heart failure.
PG  - 148-53
AB  - Recent research in the pathophysiology of congestive heart failure has focused on 
      the blockade of neurohormonal systems. Large clinical trials have clearly 
      demonstrated morbidity and mortality benefits of angiotensin-converting-enzyme 
      inhibitors and beta blockers. Indeed, all patients with heart failure should be 
      treated with these agents unless there is a specific contraindication otherwise. 
      Despite this treatment, however, mortality from heart failure remains high. 
      Current investigation is now focused on other pathophysiological mechanisms and 
      the interruption of these pathways.
