TI  - How to prevent, recognize, and treat drug-induced nephrotoxicity.
PG  - 289-90, 293-4, 296-7 passim
AB  - Many drugs can injure the kidneys, but they cause renal injury via only a few 
      common mechanisms. Many patients who develop renal injury after drug exposure 
      have identifiable risk factors that could be modified or that should preclude the 
      use of these drugs in the first place.
