TI  - Diagnosis and management of lupus pleuritis.
PG  - 312-6
AB  - Systemic lupus erythematosus is a chronic inflammatory autoimmune disorder that 
      can affect any organ system. Predominant manifestations include arthralgia, rash, 
      photosensitivity, pleuritis, renal and central nervous system involvement. 
      Fortunately, pleuritis in systemic lupus erythematosus is not usually as life 
      threatening as may be the renal or central nervous system complications. 
      Nevertheless, pleuritis does occur in systemic lupus erythematosus and may be a 
      significant cause of morbidity. In addition to primary pleuritis attributed to 
      systemic lupus erythematosus, secondary pleural complications, especially 
      infections, may occur as a consequence of systemic lupus erythematosus. Pleuritis 
      in patients with systemic lupus erythematosus may therefore frequently challenge 
      the diagnostic and therapeutic acumen of physicians.
