TI  - Initial findings of the AASK: African Americans with hypertensive kidney disease 
      benefit from an ACE inhibitor.
PG  - 304-5, 309-10, 312
AB  - Experts have long thought that African Americans were less responsive to ACE 
      inhibitors than other racial or ethnic groups. The African American Study of 
      Kidney Disease and Hypertension (AASK) provides the first evidence of a 
      beneficial effect of ACE inhibition on renal function in African American 
      patients, in addition to excellent blood pressure control.
