VI  - 5
IP  - 4
DP  - 2003 Aug
TI  - Management of diabetic and hypertensive cardiovascular disease.
PG  - 309-15
AB  - The simultaneous occurrence of essential hypertension and diabetes mellitus is 
      exceedingly common. In recent years the treatment of the cardiovascular and renal 
      complications has not only become more specific but more effective. The 
      evidence-based medicine data have been provided through many large multicenter 
      studies and strongly support the promise not only of effective treatment in 
      retarding the progression of target-organ involvement, but also the potential of 
      reversal. These dramatic therapeutic improvements have been made possible by 
      wedding the involved pathophysiologic disease mechanisms with the actions of 
      pharmacologic agents. Inherent in this concept is the promise of retarding the 
      development of the cardiovascular and renal morbid events and also reducing their 
      associated mortal endpoints.
