IS  - 0954-6820 (Linking)
VI  - 238
IP  - 2
DP  - 1995 Aug
TI  - Angio-oedema induced by enalapril.
PG  - 179-81
AB  - We report the case of a patient who, 9 months after initiation of enalapril and 
      hydrochlorothiazide combination treatment for hypertension, developed 
      angio-oedema with near fatal outcome. Our patient was successfully intubated 
      using a flexible bronchofiberoscope. This case demonstrates that patients given 
      an angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor may develop serious facial and 
      laryngeal swelling even several months after the initiation of treatment. The 
      occurrence of even mild swelling should lead to prompt cessation of the drug. 
      Patients with incipient ACE inhibitor-related angio-oedema should, without any 
      delay, be referred to hospital for emergency treatment.
