AB  - Angioedema is a well-known complication of medical therapy with 
      angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitors. Isolated uvular angioedema, a 
      rare presentation of angioedema, in a patient taking lisinopril (Zestril) is 
      described in this case report. Management of uvular edema is also reviewed.
