VI  - 18
IP  - 1
DP  - 1995 May
TI  - Pharmacologic management of congestive heart failure.
PG  - 32-44
AB  - This article is a review of the pharmacologic management of congestive heart 
      failure (CHF) and a summary of the medical literature that guides current 
      treatment strategies. Despite advances in the treatment of CHF, it remains a 
      common diagnosis with a poor prognosis. Because CHF is a progressive syndrome 
      with heterogeneous features of cardiac dysfunction, effective management requires 
      combination therapies and evolving treatment strategies. The mechanism of action, 
      goals of therapy, and demonstrated efficacy of each of the various agents used in 
      the treatment of CHF are discussed.
