DP  - 1994
TI  - Acute tubular necrosis in kidney transplant patients treated with enalapril.
PG  - 419-23
AB  - We report two cases of acute renal failure in renal transplant patients using 
      cyclosporine-A (CsA) after the introduction of angiotensin-converting enzyme 
      inhibitor (ACEI) to control arterial hypertension. They had no renal artery 
      stenosis or acute rejection. Both patients presented severe acute tubular 
      necrosis (ATN), which subsided after discontinuation of the ACEI. Synergistic 
      toxic effect of ACEI and CsA on the renal tubules might explain ATN in these two 
      cases.
