IS  - 0001-5792 (Linking)
VI  - 90
IP  - 4
DP  - 1993
TI  - Angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibition and anaemia in renal patients.
PG  - 202-5
AB  - A 35-year-old renal transplant patient with stable renal function developed an 
      unexplained anaemia. Appropriate investigations proved non-diagnostic. Only when 
      enalapril therapy was stopped did the anaemia reverse and haemoglobin levels 
      returned to pre-treatment levels. An association between angiotensin-converting 
      enzyme inhibitors and anaemia in patients with renal failure is becoming more 
      evident. A literature review of this problem and its possible pathogenesis in 
      patients with renal failure is given.
