TI  - Captopril-induced bone marrow suppression in two cardiac patients with trisomy 
      21.
PG  - 227-9
AB  - Neutropenia is an infrequent complication following administration of the 
      angiotensin-converting enzyme (ACE) inhibitor, captopril. Most reports have been 
      in adult patients, with rare reports in the pediatric population. We report two 
      cases of neutropenia following captopril use in cardiac patients with trisomy 21. 
      As this was not seen in patients without Down's syndrome, we postulate that 
      patients with trisomy 21 have bone marrow which is "at risk" for suppression, 
      and, thus warrant close evaluation while on such medications.
