TI  - Advantages and disadvantages of combining sedative agents.
PG  - 903-12
AB  - One advantage of combination sedative therapy is the use of small doses of agents 
      from different drug classes to treat concomitant behavioral problems. The 
      simultaneous use of multiple sedative agents results in the need for new clinical 
      decisions regarding the administration of and weaning from the pharmacologic 
      effects of these drugs. This article reviews the current status of research 
      regarding combination sedative therapy.
