PMID- 8645078
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 19960715
LR  - 20190704
IS  - 0004-0010 (Print)
IS  - 0004-0010 (Linking)
VI  - 131
IP  - 6
DP  - 1996 Jun
TI  - Captopril-associated "pseudocholangitis'. A case report and review of the 
      literature.
PG  - 670-1
AB  - Captopril, a competitive inhibitor of angiotensin-converting enzyme, is widely 
      used in the treatment of hypertension and heart failure. Captopril is known to be 
      associated with dermatologic, hematologic, and pulmonary adverse effects. 
      However, hepatotoxicity is extremely rare. A patient with severe cholestatic 
      jaundice induced by captopril is presented. On admission to the hospital, the 
      patient was diagnosed and treated as having cholangitis. Review of the literature 
      showed similar occurrences in other patients. Patients treated with captopril who 
      develop "atypical cholangitis" should be suspected of having captopril-associated 
      liver damage.
