TI  - Functional significance of alterations in cardiac contractile protein isoforms.
PG  - 9-18
AB  - Multiple closely related, yet distinct, isoforms exist for each of the cardiac 
      contractile proteins. The isoform composition of the heart changes in response to 
      developmental and physiologic cues. This paper reviews the molecular basis for 
      cardiac contractile protein isoform diversity and the functional consequences of 
      isoform shifts.
