DP  - 1997 Mar
TI  - Ramipril-associated lichen planus pemphigoides.
PG  - 412-4
AB  - We report the first case of lichen planus pemphigoides (LPP) secondary to 
      ingestion of ramipril, an angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitor. Clinical, 
      histological and immunofluorescent findings were all consistent with a diagnosis 
      of LPP. Linear basement membrane zone (BMZ) staining with IgG and C3 was only 
      seen at the roof of split-skin preparations and circulating autoantibody to the 
      BMZ was present at a titre of 1/100. Controlled immunoblotting of epidermal 
      extracts detected the bullous pemphigoid antigens of 230 and 180 kDa.
