TI  - Therapy of congestive heart failure in elderly persons.
PG  - 639-47
AB  - LVEF should be measured in all elderly persons with CHF Underlying causes and 
      precipitating causes of CHF should be treated. Persons with CHF associated with 
      abnormal LVEF should be treated with a low sodium diet, diuretics, and ACE 
      inhibitors. If CHF persists, digoxin should be added. If CHF still persists, 
      isosorbide dinitrate plus hydralazine should be added. If CHF still persists, a 
      beta blocker should also be added. However, calcium channel blockers should not 
      be used. Persons with CHF associated with normal LVEF should be treated with a 
      low sodium diet, diuretics, and ACE inhibitors. If CHF persists, a beta blocker, 
      isosorbide dinitrate plus hydralazine, or a calcium channel blocker should be 
      added to the therapeutic regimen. If sinus rhythm is present, digoxin should not 
      be used. Persons with CHF and abnormal or normal LVEF unable to tolerate ACE 
      inhibitors should be treated with losartan.
