DP  - 1997 Nov
TI  - Cyclosporine-induced hypertension in cardiac transplantation.
PG  - 1347-57
AB  - Cyclosporine-induced hypertension occurs in more than 90% of patients following 
      cardiac transplantation. This article underlines the clinical characteristics as 
      well as the mechanisms that can be associated with the development of 
      cyclosporine-induced hypertension. In addition, the clinical trials up to date 
      for the treatment of hypertension following cardiac transplantation are 
      discussed. However, in view of the possible long-term sequelae associated with 
      cyclosporine-induced hypertension, further studies to evaluate the long-term 
      efficacy and safety of antihypertensive agents and finally the long-term effects 
      of hypertension on the cardiac allograft are needed.
