TI  - An open trial of lisinopril ('ZESTRIL') in mild to moderate hypertension in 
      Nigeria.
PG  - 218-22
AB  - Fifty-one native Nigerian patients with mild to moderate essential hypertension 
      received Lisinopril ('Zestril') in doses of 10 mg to 40 mg once daily. All 
      patients received an initial dose of 10 mg, which was titrated up to a maximum of 
      40 mg if normotensive diastolic blood pressure had not been achieved. Reduction 
      in mean diastolic blood pressure, when compared with baseline data, was 
      significant (p < 0.001) following 16 weeks of treatment. Of the 46 evaluable 
      patients, 32 (70%) had their blood pressure controlled (i.e. diastolic blood 
      pressure < or = 90 Hg). Lisinopril ('Zestril') was well tolerated, with 27% of 
      patients reporting adverse reactions of which cough was the most common. In 
      conclusion, this study shows that Lisinopril ('Zestril"), when administered to 
      Nigerian patients, is a clinically effective and well-tolerated for mild to 
      Customer to supply Mss.
