TI  - Acute and chronic kidney disease.
PG  - 211-36
AB  - The presentation of many renal diseases in older adults is remarkably similar to 
      that in younger patients, although the symptoms and clinical findings are 
      frequently attributed to diseases of aging. Since older patients often respond to 
      treatment as well as younger patients do, they deserve a thorough investigation, 
      including renal biopsy when indicated. It is important to base decisions 
      regarding access to evaluation and treatment, quality of life, and initiation of 
      termination of dialysis on strong moral and ethical grounds.
