TI  - Effect of benazepril on complex ventricular arrhythmias in older patients with 
      congestive heart failure, prior myocardial infarction, and normal left 
      ventricular ejection fraction.
PG  - 1368-70
AB  - Sixty patients, mean age 82 +/- 8 years, with congestive heart failure, prior 
      myocardial infarction, normal left ventricular ejection fraction, and > or = 30 
      ventricular premature complexes per hour detected by 24-hour ambulatory 
      electrocardiograms, and who were treated with diuretics, were randomized to 
      treatment with benazepril 20 to 40 mg/day (30 patients) or to no benazepril (30 
      patients). At a median of 6 months after treatment, follow-up 24-hour ambulatory 
      electrocardiograms showed that compared with no benazepril, benazepril caused no 
      significant reduction in the number of ventricular premature complexes per hour 
      or in the number of runs of ventricular tachycardia per 24 hours.
