TI  - Results of the ATLAS study. High or low doses of ACE inhibitors for heart 
      failure?
PG  - 539-42
AB  - In a large, randomized study, patients with heart failure who received a large 
      daily dose of an angiotensin-converting inhibitor had a trend toward a lower 
      mortality rate than did patients who received a low daily dose. Moreover, the 
      hospitalization rate was lower in the high-dose group, and the side-effect 
      profile was the same in both groups. Physicians should try to give maximal doses 
      to achieve optimum benefit in this patient population.
